
[size=6][b][color=#FFA03C]XPortalNetworks[/color][/b][/size]

An [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/valheim/mods/170]AnyPortal[/url] revamp.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Vapok/XPortalNetworks/main/images/controller.gif[/img]


[size=6][b][color=#FFA03C]Description[/color][/b][/size]

XPortalNetworks lets you select a portal destination from a list of existing portals. 

No more tag pairing, and no more portal hubs!


[size=6][b][color=#FFA03C]Features[/color][/b][/size]

[size=3][b][color=#FFA03C]Select a destination[/color][/b][/size]

When interacting with a portal, instead of entering a tag which has to match another portal's, XPortalNetworks lets you choose the portal's destination from a list.
For your convenience, this list also shows you how far away the portals are.

[size=3][b][color=#FFA03C]Default destination[/color][/b][/size]

A Portal can be marked as the "Default Portal". When a Default Portal has been set, all newly built portals will immediately connect with that portal, without you having to go into the portal configuration panel.

[size=3][b][color=#FFA03C]Longer names[/color][/b][/size]

XPortalNetworks completely removes the character length restriction on portal names, so that you can give your portals clear and descriptive titles.

[size=3][b][color=#FFA03C]Ping a portal location[/color][/b][/size]

Forgot where you put your portal? You don't need to teleport to it to find out. Just click the Ping button next to the list, and XPortalNetworks will show the selected portal on your map, while also pinging its location to all players on the server.

If you prefer to play without a map, this button can be hidden, either by using the [font=Courier New][b]'nomap'[/b][/font] global key, or by setting [font=Courier New][b]'PingMapDisabled'[/b][/font] to [font=Courier New][b]'True'[/b][/font].

[size=3][b][color=#FFA03C]Multiplayer[/color][/b][/size]

XPortalNetworks has been built with multiplayer support at its core. All players must run the same version of XPortalNetworks. If you play on a dedicated server, that too needs to have same version of XPortalNetworks installed.

[size=3][b][color=#FFA03C]Gamepad support[/color][/b][/size]

The XPortalNetworks UI will respond to gamepad input when configuring your portal. As of v1.2.10 it even shows you the gamepad keyhints!

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SpikeHimself/XPortal/main/images/ui-keyhints-small.png[/img]

The controls are as follows:

[list]
[*][font=Courier New][b]'A'[/b][/font] / [font=Courier New][b]'Cross'[/b][/font] - Submit (i.e. press the OK button)
[*][font=Courier New][b]'B'[/b][/font]/ [font=Courier New][b]'Circle'[/b][/font] - Cancel
[*][font=Courier New][b]'Y'[/b][/font] / [font=Courier New][b]'Triangle'[/b][/font] - Ping the selected portal
[*][font=Courier New][b]'X'[/b][/font] / [font=Courier New][b]'Square'[/b][/font] - Show/hide the contents of the dropdown
[*][font=Courier New][b]'D-Pad Up'[/b][/font] / [font=Courier New][b]'D-Pad Down'[/b][/font] - Select the previous / next item in the dropdown
[/list]

[size=3][b][color=#FFA03C]Mod compatibility and integration[/color][/b][/size]

XPortalNetworks has been made fully compatible with the following mods:

[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/valheim/mods/102]Nexus Update Check[/url] by aedenthorn
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/valheim/mods/847]VHVR - Valheim VR[/url] by Flatscreen to VR Modders
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/valheim/mods/2007]Stone Portal[/url] by Jere Kuusela
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/valheim/mods/2187]Advanced Portals[/url] by Randy Knapp
[/list]
Furthermore, XPortalNetworks has a configuration option to fully integrate with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/valheim/mods/2187]Advanced Portals[/url]. If you set [font=Courier New][b]'DisplayPortalColour'[/b][/font] to [font=Courier New][b]'True'[/b][/font], each portal in XPortalNetworks's dropdown list will be prepended by a ">>" tag that has the same colour as the light that the portal emits. As of v1.2.10, Stone Portals also get their own colour!

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SpikeHimself/XPortal/main/images/advancedportals-small.png[/img]

XPortalNetworks is known to be fully incompatible with:

[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/valheim/mods/170]AnyPortal[/url] by sweetgiorni
[*][url=https://github.com/redseiko/ValheimMods/releases]ComfyGizmo[/url] by redseiko
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/valheim/mods/184]Custom Meshes[/url] by aedenthorn
[/list]

[size=6][b][color=#FFA03C]Configuration[/color][/b][/size]

XPortalNetworks's config file, which can be found at [font=Courier New][b]'Valheim\BepInEx\config\vapok.mods.xportalnetworks.cfg'[/b][/font], contains the following settings:

[font=Courier New][b]'PingMapDisabled'[/b][/font]

Disable the Ping Map button completely. For players who wish to play without a map. This setting is owned by the server: it is synchronized to all clients and can only be changed by server admins.

[font=Courier New][b]'DisplayPortalColour'[/b][/font]

Show a coloured ">>" tag in the list of portals to indicate the portal type (integration with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/valheim/mods/2187]Advanced Portals[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/valheim/mods/2007]Stone Portal[/url]).

[font=Courier New][b]'DoublePortalCosts'[/b][/font]

Since XPortalNetworks is essentially a cheat, in that you only need half the amount of portals now, this setting allows you to compensate for that by doubling portal costs. This setting is owned by the server: it is synchronized to all clients and can only be changed by server admins.

[font=Courier New][b]'HidePortalDistance'[/b][/font]

If you don't want to see how far away the portals in the list are, you can use this option to remove that. This setting is owned by the server: it is synchronized to all clients and can only be changed by server admins.

[font=Courier New][b]'DefaultPortal'[/b][/font]

This configuration option exists to save your personal Default Portal. Its value will be set by checking the Default Portal checkbox on the portal configuration panel. This value should not be manually edited in the file.

[font=Courier New][b]'DefaultPrivatePortal'[/b][/font]

If true, newly placed portals start as private (owner-only). If false, they start public on the Global network until changed.

[font=Courier New][b]'RestrictPortalRemoval'[/b][/font]

Restricts removing a portal with the hammer to the player who placed it, or to server admins. Other removal (such as structural damage) is unaffected. This setting is owned by the server: it is synchronized to all clients and can only be changed by server admins.

[font=Courier New][b]'AdminsSeeAllNetworks'[/b][/font]

When disabled (the default), server admins and the host are treated like normal players and only see and use unrestricted portal networks, or networks they are members of. When enabled, they can see and use every network. This setting is owned by the server: it is synchronized to all clients and can only be changed by server admins.

[font=Courier New][b]'Portal Networks'[/b][/font]

The [font=Courier New][b]'[Portal Networks]'[/b][/font] section defines up to 15 custom networks. Each one has two settings: [font=Courier New][b]'Network 1 Name'[/b][/font] and [font=Courier New][b]'Network 1 Allow List'[/b][/font] (for the first network; the number runs from 1 to 15). Leave a name empty to keep that slot unused, and leave the allow list empty to let everyone use the network. The allow list takes comma separated player ids, such as [font=Courier New][b]'Steam_12345678901234567'[/b][/font]. These settings are owned by the server: they are synchronized to all clients and can only be changed by server admins - which means networks can be added, renamed and restricted from inside the game, through the ConfigurationManager window.

[font=Courier New][b]'Show Splash on Startup'[/b][/font]

If enabled, displays the mod overview and links splash screen on game startup.

[font=Courier New][b]'Enable Anonymous Telemetry'[/b][/font]

If enabled, sends anonymous mod launch and heartbeat telemetry to help improve mod stability and track active versions.


[size=6][b][color=#FFA03C]Installation instructions[/color][/b][/size]

XPortalNetworks is a [url=https://valheim.thunderstore.io/package/denikson/BepInExPack_Valheim/]BepInEx[/url] plugin. As such, you must have BepInEx installed. Most other Valheim mods are also BepInEx plugins, so chances are you already have this.

XPortalNetworks makes use of the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/valheim/mods/1138]Jotunn[/url] library, so you must install that before installing XPortalNetworks. If you do not install Jotunn, XPortalNetworks will simply not be loaded by your game and it will not work.

I very strongly recommend using a mod manager such as [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/site/mods/1]Vortex[/url] or [url=https://valheim.thunderstore.io/package/ebkr/r2modman/]r2modman[/url]. They will take care of everything for you and you don't have to worry about which files go where. I recommend against manual installation.
[list=1]
[*]Make sure you have [url=https://valheim.thunderstore.io/package/denikson/BepInExPack_Valheim/]BepInEx[/url] installed.
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/valheim/mods/1138]Jotunn[/url].
[*]On [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/valheim/mods/3719]Nexus Mods[/url] click 'Mod manager download', or on [url=https://valheim.thunderstore.io/package/Vapok/XPortalNetworks/]Thunderstore[/url] click 'Install with Mod Manager'.
[/list]

To install XPortalNetworks on a dedicated server, copy all of the contents of the [font=Courier New][b]'plugins\'[/b][/font] directory found inside the .zip file download to the  [font=Courier New][b]'Valheim\BepInEx\plugins\'[/b][/font] directory on your server. 


[size=6][b][color=#FFA03C]Bugs, Feature Requests and Translations[/color][/b][/size]

First of all, before you report a bug, please make sure that the problem you are experiencing is actually caused by XPortalNetworks. If you are running other mods, disable those, and see if the problem goes away. Or the other way around: disable XPortalNetworks, and see if that makes the problem go away. If you discover that XPortalNetworks is incompatible with another mod, please do report that, because I might be able to create work-arounds for that. If you are not sure, or you are struggling with these steps, then just report the problem, and we'll go from there.

It is important to me that I can make XPortalNetworks as bug-free as possible, but [b]please bear in mind that without your [font=Courier New][b]'LogOutput.log'[/b][/font], I will not be able to debug your issue at all[/b]. Just showing me a screenshot of an error is not enough for me to discover the cause of that error.

[size=4][b]If you have issues or feedback, please use XPortalNetworks's [url=https://github.com/Vapok/XPortalNetworks]GitHub page[/url].[/b][/size]

To report a bug, please navigate to the [url=https://github.com/Vapok/XPortalNetworks/issues]Issues page[/url], click [url=https://github.com/Vapok/XPortalNetworks/issues/new/choose]New issue[/url], choose [font=Courier New][b]'Bug report'[/b][/font], and fill out the template.

For feature requests, choose [font=Courier New][b]'Feature request'[/b][/font] on the [url=https://github.com/Vapok/XPortalNetworks/issues/new/choose]New issue[/url] page.

To add a translation to XPortalNetworks, choose [font=Courier New][b]'Translation'[/b][/font] when submitting a [url=https://github.com/Vapok/XPortalNetworks/issues/new/choose]New issue[/url].


